cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use forenix-oss in academic work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "forenix-oss: an open-source platform for lawful OSINT and forensic case management"
abstract: >-
  forenix-oss is an open-source, MIT-licensed platform that
  operationalises the question of how OSINT pipelines can be
  structured to produce trustworthy, legally admissible evidence
  while safeguarding fundamental rights. It ships a SHA-256
  forward-chained audit log, three independent attestation
  backends (local HMAC, GitHub-issue witness, Sigstore Rekor), a
  structured-analytic-technique scaffold grounded in the
  Coulthart and Heuer-Pherson literature, a real Git repository
  per forensic case, and a free-adapter substrate spanning six
  large language model backends.
